" and |=5|+") f|=49|+[[|=9|+]]|=118|+[[|=6|+]]|=72|+[[|=a|+]]|=11|+[[|=e|+]]|=43|+[[|=2|+ (Unix)%7Ced]]|=119|+[[|=11|+]]|=169|+[[|=a|+]]|=1d|+[[|=5|+ (Unix)%7Cpatch]]|=1|+ |=50|+<ref>{{cite newsgroup%0A %7C title %3D A patch applier%2D%2DYOU WANT THIS!!!%0A %7C author %3D Larry Wall%0A %7C date %3D November 9, 1984%0A %7C newsgroup %3D net.sources%0A %7C message%2Did %3D 1457@sdcrdcf.UUCP%0A %7C url %3D https://groups.google.com/d/msg/net.sources/qtfVio1sSHs/G0cPT5HFDFcJ%0A %7C access%2Ddate %3D May 11, 2015%0A }}</ref><ref>{{cite newsgroup%0A %7C title %3D patch version 1.2%2D%2DYOU WANT THIS%0A %7C author %3D Larry Wall%0A %7C date %3D November 29, 1984%0A %7C newsgroup %3D net.sources%0A %7C message%2Did %3D 1508@sdcrdcf.UUCP%0A %7C url %3D https://groups.google.com/d/msg/net.sources/uWFr9NOp_fw/SRS_P2vSgFgJ%0A %7C access%2Ddate %3D May 11, 2015%0A }}</ref><ref>{{cite newsgroup%0A %7C title %3D patch version 1.3%0A %7C author %3D Larry Wall%0A %7C date %3D May 8, 1985%0A %7C newsgroup %3D net.sources%0A %7C message%2Did %3D 813@genrad.UUCP%0A %7C url %3D https://groups.google.com/d/msg/mod.sources/xSQM63e39YY/apNNJSkJi0gJ%0A %7C access%2Ddate %3D May 11, 2015%0A }}</ref>%0A|=6c|+[[|=5|+]]|=1c9|+[[|=1a|+]]|=cc|+[[|=22|+]]|=1|+<ref name%3D"diff paper" />|=2ac|+. In this case it is|=3|+       a b c d  f  g  j  z|=cc|+(as indicated by the '%2D' marks, below).|=6b|+ (as indicated by the '%2B' marks).|=3|+       e   h i   q   k r x y%0A        %2B   %2D %2B   %2D   %2B %2B %2B %2B|=24e|+{{Col%2Dbegin}}%0A{{Col%2Dbreak%7Cwidth%3D33%25}}%0A''original'':%0A<source lang%3D"text" line>%0AThis part of the%0Adocument has stayed the%0Asame from version to%0Aversion.  It shouldn't%0Abe shown if it doesn't%0Achange.  Otherwise, that%0Awould not be helping to%0Acompress the size of the%0Achanges.%0A%0AThis paragraph contains%0Atext that is outdated.%0AIt will be deleted in the%0Anear future.%0A%0AIt is important to spell%0Acheck this dokument. On%0Athe other hand, a%0Amisspelled word isn't%0Athe end of the world.%0ANothing in the rest of%0Athis paragraph needs to%0Abe changed. Things can%0Abe added after it.%0A</source>%0A{{col%2Dbreak}}%0A''new'':%0A<source lang%3D"text" line>%0AThis is an important%0Anotice! It should%0Atherefore be located at%0Athe beginning of this%0Adocument!%0A%0AThis part of the%0Adocument has stayed the%0Asame from version to%0Aversion.  It shouldn't%0Abe shown if it doesn't%0Achange.  Otherwise, that%0Awould not be helping to%0Acompress the size of the%0Achanges.%0A%0AIt is important to spell%0Acheck this document. On%0Athe other hand, a%0Amisspelled word isn't%0Athe end of the world.%0ANothing in the rest of%0Athis paragraph needs to%0Abe changed. Things can%0Abe added after it.%0A%0AThis paragraph contains%0Aimportant new additions%0Ato this document.%0A</source>%0A{{col%2Dbreak%7Cwidth%3D33%25}}%0AThe command '''<tt>diff original new</tt>''' produces the following ''normal diff output'':%0A{{pre%7C%0A0a1,6%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C> This is an important%0A> notice! It should%0A> therefore be located at%0A> the beginning of this%0A> document!%0A>}}%0A11,15d16%0A{{font color%7Cdarkred%7C< This paragraph contains%0A< text that is outdated.%0A< It will be deleted in the%0A< near future.%0A<}}%0A17c18%0A{{font color%7Cdarkred%7C< check this dokument. On}}%0A%2D%2D%2D%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C> check this document. On}}%0A24a26,29%0A{{font color%7Cdarkgreen%7C>%0A> This paragraph contains%0A> important new additions%0A> to this document.}}}}%0A%0A{{Note2}} ''Here, the diff output is shown with colors to make it easier to read. The diff utility does not produce colored output; its output is [[plain text]]. However, many tools can show the output with colors by using [[syntax highlighting]].''%0A{{col%2Dend}}|=10f|+[[Less%2Dthan sign%7C|=9|+]]|=5|+[[Greater%2Dthan sign%7C|=c|+]]|=1a6|+<ref>{{cite book%7Ctitle%3DComparing and Merging Files with GNU Diff and Patch%7Curl%3Dhttps://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/%7Cauthor1%3DDavid MacKenzie %7Cauthor2%3DPaul Eggert %7Cauthor3%3DRichard Stallman %7Cisbn%3D0%2D9541617%2D5%2D0%7Cpublisher%3DNetwork Theory%7Cyear%3D1997%7Clocation%3DBristol}}</ref>|=10d|+(ND)|=3d|+<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor%3DE. Myers%7Ctitle%3DAn O(ND) Difference Algorithm and Its Variations%7Cjournal%3DAlgorithmica%7Cvolume%3D1%7Cissue%3D2%7Cyear%3D1986%7Cpages%3D251–266%7Curl%3Dhttp://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi%3D10.1.1.4.6927%7Cdoi%3D10.1007/BF01840446}}</ref> |=3e|+<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor1%3DWebb Miller %7Cauthor2%3DEugene W. Myers %7Ctitle%3DA File Comparison Program%7Cjournal%3DSoftware &#x2014; Practice and Experience%7Cvolume%3D15%7Cissue%3D11%7Cyear%3D1985%7Cpages%3D1025&#x2013;1040%7Cdoi%3D10.1002/spe.4380151102}}</ref> |=6f|+[[|=c|+]]|=1|+<ref>{{cite journal%7Cauthor%3DEsko Ukkonen%7Ctitle%3DAlgorithms for Approximate String Matching%7Cvolume%3D64%7Cjournal%3DInformation and Control%7Cissue%3D1%2D3%7Cyear%3D1985%7Cpages%3D100&#x2013;118 %7C doi %3D 10.1016/S0019%2D9958(85)80046%2D2}}</ref>|=67|+[[|=7|+]]|=a0|+[[Ed (text editor)%7C|=b|+]]|=85|+ows:|=3|+24a%0A %0A This paragraph contains%0A important new additions%0A to this document.%0A .%0A 17c%0A check this document. On%0A .%0A 11,15d%0A 0a%0A This is an important%0A notice! It should%0A therefore be located at%0A the beginning of this%0A document!%0A %0A .|=105|+{{code%7Clang%3Dbash%7Cprintf "w\nq\n" >> mydiff}}|=66|+{{code%7Clang%3Dbash%7Ced %2Ds original < mydiff}}|=1e|+[[BSD%7C|=1d|+]]|=2f|+({{code%7C%2Dc}})|=3e|+ ({{code%7C%2Dr}}),|=7a3|+<source lang%3D"diff">%0A*** /path/to/original%09timestamp%0A%2D%2D%2D /path/to/new%09timestamp%0A***************%0A*** 1,3 ****%0A%2D%2D%2D 1,9 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A%2B This is an important%0A%2B notice! It should%0A%2B therefore be located at%0A%2B the beginning of this%0A%2B document!%0A%2B%0A  This part of the%0A  document has stayed the%0A  same from version to%0A***************%0A*** 8,20 ****%0A  compress the size of the%0A  changes.%0A%0A%2D This paragraph contains%0A%2D text that is outdated.%0A%2D It will be deleted in the%0A%2D near future.%0A%0A  It is important to spell%0A! check this dokument. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of the world.%0A%2D%2D%2D 14,21 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A  compress the size of the%0A  changes.%0A%0A  It is important to spell%0A! check this document. On%0A  the other hand, a%0A  misspelled word isn't%0A  the end of the world.%0A***************%0A*** 22,24 ****%0A%2D%2D%2D 23,29 %2D%2D%2D%2D%0A  this paragraph needs to%0A  be changed. Things can%0A  be added after it.%0A%2B%0A%2B This paragraph contains%0A%2B important new additions%0A%2B to this document.%0A</source>%0A%0A|=10b|+[[|=13|+]]|=2c|+[[|=6|+(Unix)%7Cpatch]] |=ed|+[[|=d|+]]|=55|+[[|=10|+]]|=23|+[[GNU%7C|=b|+]]|=ef|+[[Header (computing)%7C|=6|+]]|=45|+"<tt>%2D%2D%2D</tt>" |=20|-1|+"<tt>%2B%2B%2B</tt>".%0A|=c5|+[[|=9|+]]|=27|+[[|=a|+]]|=c9|+[[|=7|+]]|=40|+the|=1|+context format ([[#Context format%7Cabove]]).%0A|=31|-4|+llows:|=3|+@@ %2Dl,s %2Bl,s @@ ''optional section heading''|=4c3|+[[|=12|+]]|=a|+<ref>[https://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/manual/html_node/Sections.html 2.2.3 Showing Which Sections Differences Are in], GNU diffutils manual</ref>|=bf|+<ref>[http://www.artima.com/weblogs/viewpost.jsp?thread%3D164293 Unified Diff Format] by [[Guido van Rossum]], June 14, 2006</ref>|=2e|+:|=3|+%2Dcheck this dokument. On%0A %2Bcheck this document. On|=4b|+<source lang%3D"diff">%0A%2D%2D%2D /path/to/original%09timestamp%0A%2B%2B%2B /path/to/new%09timestamp%0A@@ %2D1,3 %2B1,9 @@%0A%2BThis is an important%0A%2Bnotice! It should%0A%2Btherefore be located at%0A%2Bthe beginning of this%0A%2Bdocument!%0A%2B%0A This part of the%0A document has stayed the%0A same from version to%0A@@ %2D8,13 %2B14,8 @@%0A compress the size of the%0A changes.%0A%0A%2DThis paragraph contains%0A%2Dtext that is outdated.%0A%2DIt will be deleted in the%0A%2Dnear future.%0A%2D%0A It is important to spell%0A%2Dcheck this dokument. On%0A%2Bcheck this document. On%0A the other hand, a%0A misspelled word isn't%0A the end of the world.%0A@@ %2D22,3 %2B23,7 @@%0A this paragraph needs to%0A be changed. Things can%0A be added after it.%0A%2B%0A%2BThis paragraph contains%0A%2Bimportant new additions%0A%2Bto this document.%0A</source>|=17a|+[[|=10|+]]|=13|+[[|=a|+ (software)%7CSubversion]]|=11b|+:|=3|+Index: path/to/file.cpp|=f1|+<ref>http://pubs.opengroup.org/onlinepubs/9699919799/basedefs/V1_chap03.html#tag_03_205 Section 3.206</ref>|=6|+[[Patch (Unix)%7C|=5|+]]|=11e|+{{citation needed%7Cdate%3DFebruary 2015}}|=2|+[[|=5|+]]|=ca|+[[|=1|+evision |=1|+ontrol |=1|+ystem%7CRCS]]|=1|+<ref>https://www.gnu.org/software/rcs/manual/merge.html</ref>|=5|+[[merge (revision control)%7C|=7|+]]|=56|+[[Patch (Unix)%7C|=5|+]]|=14|+[[|=5|+]]|=5|+[[|=5|+]]|=114|+[[|=5|+]]<ref>https://www.gnu.org/software/wdiff/</ref>|=12e|+<ref>https://www.colordiff.org/</ref>|=8c|+<ref>{{cite journal%7Clast1%3DHorwitz%7Cfirst1%3DSusan%7Ctitle%3DIdentifying the semantic and textual differences between two versions of a program%7Cjournal%3DACM SIGPLAN Notices%7Cdate%3DJune 1990%7Cvolume%3D25%7Cissue%3D6%7Cpages%3D234–245%7Cdoi%3D10.1145/93548.93574%7Curl%3Dhttp://www.cs.wisc.edu/wpis/papers/sigplan90.ps}}</ref><ref>{{cite journal%7Clast1%3DYang%7Cfirst1%3DWuu%7Ctitle%3DIdentifying syntactic differences between two programs%7Cjournal%3DSoftware: Practice and Experience%7Cdate%3DJuly 1991%7Cvolume%3D21%7Cissue%3D7%7Cpages%3D739–755%7Cdoi%3D10.1002/spe.4380210706}}</ref><ref>Grass. Cdiff: A syntax directed Diff for C%2B%2B programs. Proceedings USENIX C%2B%2B Conf., pp. 181%2D193, 1992</ref>|=28|+<ref>Compare%2B%2B, http://www.coodesoft.com/</ref><ref>SmartDifferencer, http://www.semanticdesigns.com/Products/SmartDifferencer</ref><ref>Cheney, Austin. ''Pretty Diff %2D Documentation''. http://prettydiff.com/documentation.php</ref>|=1d|+<ref>''DaisyDiff'', https://code.google.com/p/daisydiff/</ref>|=3b|+<ref>''xmldiffpatch'', http://msdn.microsoft.com/en%2Dus/library/aa302294.aspx</ref><ref>''xmldiffmerge'', http://www.alphaworks.ibm.com/tech/xmldiffmerge</ref>|=17|+[[Computer |=4|+%7Cfile]]|=56|-1|=32|+<ref name%3D"dontcallme">{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttps://github.com/dontcallmedom/spiff%7Ctitle%3Dspiff%7Cauthor%3Ddontcallmedotcom%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref>{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttps://stackoverflow.com/a/1489107/2291035%7Cdate%3D2009%2D09%2D28%7Cauthor%3DDavide%7Ctitle%3Dstackoverflow%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref name%3D"hpux">{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttp://hpux.connect.org.uk/hppd/hpux/Text/spiff%2D1.0/%7Ctitle%3DHP%2DUX Porting and Archiving%7Clocation%3DUK%7Cfirst%3DDaniel W%7Clast%3DNachbar%7Cdate%3D1999%2D12%2D01%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D13}}</ref>|=7|+[[Space (punctuation)%7C|=a|-1|+]]<ref name%3D"dontcallme"/><ref name%3D"hpux"/>|=51|+[[|=3|+ (Unix)%7Ccmp]]|=2|+[[Telcordia Technologies%7C|=8|+]]|=1c|+<ref name%3D"dontcallme"/><ref name%3D"hpux"/>|=4|+[[|=4|+]]|=4e|+<ref>{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttp://www.math.utah.edu/cgi%2Dbin/man2html.cgi?/usr/local/man/man1/spiff.1%7Ctitle%3DSPIFF 1%7Cdate%3D1988%2D02%2D02%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref><ref>{{cite web%7Curl%3Dhttp://hpux.connect.org.uk/hppd/hpux/Text/spiff%2D1.0/man.html%7Ctitle%3DMan page%7Clocation%3DUK%7Cfirst%3DDaniel W%7Clast%3DNachbar%7Cdate%3D1988%2D02%2D02%7Caccessdate%3D2013%2D06%2D16}}</ref>|=16|+[[|=f|+]]|=33|+[[|=1|+ (programming language)%7CC]]|=2|+[[|=c|+]]|=2|+[[|=7|+]]|=2|+[[|=5|+a%2D2]] and [[Lisp (programming language)%7CLisp]] [[programming language]]s.|=2|+%3D%3DFree file comparison tools%3D%3D%0A{{colbegin}}%0A*[[cmp (Unix)%7Ccmp]]%0A*[[comm]]%0A*[[Diff%2DText]]%0A*[[diff3]]%0A*[[Kompare]]%0A*[[tkdiff]]%0A*[[WinMerge]] (Microsoft Windows)%0A*[[meld (software)%7Cmeld]]%0A*[[Pretty Diff]]%0A*[[spiff (UNIX)%7Cspiff]]%0A{{colend}}%0A%0A%3D%3DSee also%3D%3D%0A{{colbegin}}%0A*[[Comparison of file comparison tools]]%0A*[[Delta encoding]]%0A*[[Difference operator]]%0A*[[Edit distance]]%0A**[[Levenshtein distance]]%0A*[[History of software configuration management]]%0A*[[Longest common subsequence problem]]%0A*[[Microsoft File Compare]]%0A*[[Revision control]]%0A*[[Software configuration management]]%0A{{colend}}%0A%0A%3D%3DNotes%3D%3D%0A|=12|+{{cite journal%7Cauthor%3DPaul Heckel%7Ctitle%3DA technique for isolating differences between files%7Cjournal%3DCommunications of the ACM%7Cvolume%3D21%7Cissue%3D4%7Cdate%3DApril 1978%7Cpages%3D264&#x2013;268%7Cdoi%3D10.1145/359460.359467}}[http://doi.acm.org/10.1145/359460.359467]|=66|+[http://www.ioplex.com/~miallen/libmba/dl/src/diff.c |=f|+]|=15|+{{Prone to spam%7Cdate%3DMay 2012}}%0A{{Z148}}<!%2D%2D     {{No more links}}%0A%0A       Please be cautious adding more external links.%0A%0AWikipedia is not a collection of links and should not be used for advertising.%0A%0A     Excessive or inappropriate links will be removed.%0A%0A See [[Wikipedia:External links]] & [[Wikipedia:Spam]] for details.%0A%0AIf there are already suitable links, propose additions or replacements on the article's talk page, or submit your link to the relevant category at  the Open Directory Project (dmoz.org) and link there  using {{Dmoz}}.%0A%0A%2D%2D>|=2|+{{man%7Ccu%7Cdiff%7CSUS%7Ccompare two files}}|=2|+{{Dmoz%7CComputers/Software/File_Management/File_Comparison%7CFile comparison}}|=2|+[https://www.gnu.org/software/diffutils/ |=12|+]|=18|+[[|=18|+]]|=29|+[http://www.bodurov.com/JavaScriptDiff/ |=19|+]|=117|
